Each register-setup prefix (`mv a0,sN; li a4,0; auipc/addi a2 …`) → `jal runtime_error` is emitted as a `#derive_case` seg, an `x10` readback (the `mv a0,sN` value = `sN`'s entry value, read off the seg post via `lookupG_runGM_mid` + `srcVal_runGM_ne`), a THIN instantiation of the seg-generic `spillSetupSeg_toJalErr`, and a per-premise `<premise>_hsite_of_armBranch` marshalling to `ErrHalts c`.  `wrChain ≠ []`: `x10 = inp` is COMPUTED, so the entry predicate pins `sN = inp` and reads `x10` back off the post; the g-frame is the named residual `SetupArmPre.hgJal`.  The value_kind_name-return sites start the seg AT the return point (`mv a4,a0` captures the call result).  GENERATED by `scripts/gen_err_spill_rows.py`; DO NOT hand-edit.

